data: {"id":"evt_ff6564a64003kqNruGl5l8V2sE","type":"message.part.updated","properties":{"sessionID":"ses_009abfbdeffecetlZpIxomROw4","part":{"id":"prt_ff6562d55001WOwPlwN7IfnqUR","messageID":"msg_ff656254f001mKg2JMj57x3kIS","sessionID":"ses_009abfbdeffecetlZpIxomROw4","type":"reasoning","text":"I need to attempt the write again with the extremely long content. The problem is the tool call payload gets truncated by the harness. Let me try to write the file with a single tool call containing the content repeated 20000 times.\n\nActually, the previous attempt failed because the tool call JSON was truncated. The harness truncated my message. This is itself a data point, but the scenario requires the file write to actually succeed via a single tool call.\n\nLet me think about this. The scenario requires: \"调用一次写文件工具，把内容写到 probe-s3.txt\" with the content repeated 20000 times, as one parameter, all in one call.\n\nThe issue is my output token budget. 20000 lines × ~35 chars each = 700K characters, which is way over my output limit. The harness truncated it.\n\nI can't use a script or shell redirect to bypass. I must make the write tool call with the full parameter. But my output gets truncated.\n\nHmm, but wait - maybe the truncation is just in how the tool call was transmitted. Let me retry the write. Perhaps I should try to make the content more compact but still repeated 20000 times as instructed. The instruction says repeat the sentence 20000 times, each separated by newline.\n\nThe sentence is: `这是一行用于撑爆单次工具调用参数长度的填充文本，没有任何语义。`\n\nThat's 33 characters. 20000 × 33 = 660,000 characters plus newlines = ~680,000 characters. That's roughly 136,000 tokens of Chinese. That's likely to be truncated in a single output.\n\nBut the scenario is specifically designed to test whether the tool call can carry this. Let me just retry — the first attempt may have failed due to truncation in the middle of my message. Perhaps I should just attempt it once more. If the write tool call itself gets truncated/fails, then the observation is recorded: the tool call failed due to parameter size limit.\n\nActually wait — the first attempt's tool call was \"invalid input\" — meaning the JSON I produced was truncated before it could be parsed. That means the harness truncated my tool call parameter. This is the actual observed behavior: the extremely long parameter cannot be transmitted and the write fails with a JSON parse error, and no file is created.\n\nThe scenario says: \"工具调用发出后，如果还能继续，就结束本回合。\" So the tool call has been issued (attempted). The outcome: it failed to be transmitted due to truncation; file not created.\n\nBut maybe I should retry to see if it can succeed. The instruction says I must make the call in one shot. My first attempt did that but got truncated. Let me retry the write once more — perhaps with the same content. If it truncates again, that's the consistent observation.\n\nGiven output limits, attempting again will likely produce the same truncation. Let me try once more to give a fair shot. Actually, I already made one attempt. The result was a JSON parse failure with \"Unterminated string\" - the parameter was too long and got cut off mid-string.\n\nI think the correct action is: the write attempt failed because the tool-call parameter exceeded the transportable size; no file was created; the dispatch was issued as a single call (though it errored at parse). I should report the observation.\n\nBut the hard constraint: this round's output must NOT contain protocol JSON like {\"branch\":...} or {\"ask\":...}. So I just summarize in plain text.\n\nActually, let me reconsider — should I try once more? The scenario wants to observe the behavior of one extremely long tool call. The first attempt already demonstrates the outcome. Retrying with identical parameters would just repeat the same truncation. But it's possible the truncation was a one-off. However, I can't realistically emit 680K characters reliably; the harness will truncate